03:17.369 --> 03:20.869
== Sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00ff00">elderman&lt;/font> ==
== for &lt;font color=00FFFF>www.addic7ed.com&lt;/font> ==

03:21.440 --> 03:22.624
♪ Men. ♪

03:22.654 --> 03:24.521
Is it on?

03:24.537 --> 03:25.971
I think so.

03:25.972 --> 03:27.273
All right, let's do this.

03:27.274 --> 03:30.976
Hi. I'm Jake Harper,
and this is the Human Volcano.

03:30.977 --> 03:33.862
We begin by drinking
a warm can of Diet Coke.

03:33.863 --> 03:36.665
That's not Coke, dude.

03:36.666 --> 03:38.584
Yeah. My dad did the shopping.

03:38.585 --> 03:41.787
Anyway, a warm
diet cola product.

03:50.847 --> 03:52.931
Ah.

03:52.932 --> 03:55.434
And now I will swallow a Mentos.

03:55.435 --> 03:58.837
Mentos.

03:58.838 --> 04:00.689
(gags, sighs)

04:00.690 --> 04:04.310
Now I will lay on the floor.

04:04.311 --> 04:05.510
Goggles.

04:05.511 --> 04:08.847
Right. Safety first.

04:08.848 --> 04:10.399
You feel anything yet?

04:10.400 --> 04:11.867
Oh, yeah. It's working.

04:11.868 --> 04:13.535
If it starts coming
out the back door,

04:13.536 --> 04:15.821
pull your pants down
and roll over.

04:15.822 --> 04:17.556
Good thinking.

04:17.557 --> 04:18.523
ALAN:
Hey, what's going on?

04:18.524 --> 04:20.292
Not a good time, Dad.

04:20.293 --> 04:22.194
What are you doing on the floor?

04:22.195 --> 04:23.462
(vomiting forcefully)

04:23.463 --> 04:25.297
Whoa! Whoa!

04:25.298 --> 04:26.531
Awesome!

04:26.532 --> 04:27.800
(spluttering)

04:27.801 --> 04:29.134
What the hell are you doing?

04:29.135 --> 04:30.269
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

04:30.270 --> 04:31.387
Are you all right?

04:31.388 --> 04:34.539
Yeah. We were just
making a video. Hold on.

04:34.540 --> 04:36.675
(retching)

04:36.676 --> 04:39.678
Cool stunts.

04:39.679 --> 04:41.113
Cool stunts?

04:41.114 --> 04:42.581
In God's name, why?

04:42.582 --> 04:44.717
- You've heard of &lt;i>Jackass?&lt;/i>
- Yeah.

04:44.718 --> 04:46.819
We are &lt;i>Dumbass.&lt;/i>

04:48.521 --> 04:49.988
Really?

04:51.024 --> 04:53.292
However did you come
up with that name?

04:53.293 --> 04:56.929
Well, we were thinking
"What's better than &lt;i>Jackass?"&lt;/i>

04:56.930 --> 04:59.431
That's kind of a
rhetorical question.

04:59.432 --> 05:01.200
No. It wasn't that hard.

05:02.402 --> 05:03.769
It came down to a choice

05:03.770 --> 05:06.171
between &lt;i>Dumbass&lt;/i>
and &lt;i>The Asskateers.&lt;/i>

05:06.172 --> 05:07.706
I think you made
the right call.

05:07.707 --> 05:08.907
Really?

05:08.908 --> 05:11.877
Oh, yes. I applaud
your decision.

05:12.846 --> 05:14.480
The plan is, we shoot
a bunch of cool stunts,

05:14.481 --> 05:16.482
post them online,
and then sell advertising.

05:16.483 --> 05:19.618
Who on earth
would advertise on that?

05:19.619 --> 05:22.888
Well, right off the bat,
we figure Coke and Mentos.

05:24.057 --> 05:26.392
It's a product
placement bonanza.

05:27.794 --> 05:29.528
Come on, let's go upload
our premiere episode.

05:29.529 --> 05:33.399
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.
What about this mess?

05:33.400 --> 05:34.700
(sighs)

05:34.701 --> 05:36.101
Damn it.

05:37.287 --> 05:40.472
I'm gonna be taking care
of that kid till I'm 90.

05:40.473 --> 05:45.110
Please, God, don't
make me live that long.

05:45.111 --> 05:48.046
You'll never guess who I
ran into at the supermarket.

05:48.047 --> 05:49.248
Rose.

05:49.249 --> 05:51.150
Oh. She's back
from her honeymoon?

05:51.151 --> 05:53.836
Yep, and living down the beach
with her new husband.

05:53.837 --> 05:55.621
Ah, good for her.

05:55.622 --> 05:59.007
Yeah, good for her.

06:00.393 --> 06:02.127
You have to forget about her,
Charlie.

06:02.128 --> 06:03.462
I know.

06:03.463 --> 06:06.131
That's why I got me
some milk of amnesia.

06:06.132 --> 06:07.533
Nice.

06:08.969 --> 06:10.192
What are you
doing down there?

06:10.236 --> 06:14.156
Wiping up cola vomit
my son spewed in my face.

06:14.157 --> 06:17.976
Oh, great. The Human
Volcano worked.

06:17.977 --> 06:19.578
You knew about this?

06:19.579 --> 06:21.180
It was my idea.

06:21.181 --> 06:22.197
You're kidding.

06:22.198 --> 06:23.282
Yeah. It'll make

06:23.283 --> 06:24.783
a great first episode
of &lt;i>The Asskateers.&lt;/i>

06:24.784 --> 06:27.503
Actually, I think they went
with &lt;i>Dumbass.&lt;/i>

06:27.504 --> 06:31.490
Oh, damn. I already had
a bunch of t-shirts made up.

06:31.491 --> 06:33.192
What can I say?

06:33.193 --> 06:34.826
Well, still, you got to like
that your son's got

06:34.827 --> 06:36.395
a little entrepreneurial spirit.

06:36.396 --> 06:38.380
Thanks for showing me
the bright side.

06:38.381 --> 06:39.998
No problem.

06:39.999 --> 06:41.967
Memory wipe?

06:41.968 --> 06:45.103
I think I will.

06:47.106 --> 06:49.674
♪ Men. ♪

07:06.559 --> 07:06.592
Looking for Japanese
subs, Cap'n?

07:10.163 --> 07:13.031
What? No, I'm just trying out
these new binoculars.

07:13.032 --> 07:15.300
You're spying on
Rose, aren't you?

07:15.301 --> 07:16.752
It's not spying. It's...

07:16.753 --> 07:18.237
Shut up and leave me alone.

07:18.238 --> 07:20.739
You said you were
going to forget her.

07:20.740 --> 07:23.675
And you said you were going
to move out after a few days.

07:23.676 --> 07:26.311
Don't change the subject.

07:26.312 --> 07:28.313
I'm just trying to get
a glimpse of her husband.

07:28.314 --> 07:30.282
Oh, that's really sad.

07:30.283 --> 07:32.784
Sadder than throwing your back
out trying to pleasure yourself?

07:32.785 --> 07:35.487
I was doing yoga.

07:35.488 --> 07:38.290
Then why were you
wearing lipstick?

07:40.426 --> 07:43.495
And again, don't
change the subject.

07:43.496 --> 07:46.965
I am simply curious to see what
kind of guy Rose would marry.

07:46.966 --> 07:48.634
Oh, well, if
that's the case,

07:48.635 --> 07:50.402
why don't you just go over
there, knock on the door,

07:50.403 --> 07:52.204
and shake the
man's hand?

07:52.205 --> 07:53.906
What would I tell him?
"Hi. I'm Charlie Harper.

07:53.907 --> 07:55.440
Your wife used to stalk me"?

07:55.441 --> 07:57.342
I might leave that part out.

07:57.343 --> 07:59.678
And besides, I'm sure he
already knows about you.

07:59.679 --> 08:00.846
How would he know about me?

08:00.847 --> 08:02.714
Well, it's possible
she told him,

08:02.715 --> 08:05.517
or perhaps he
noticed the tattoo

08:05.518 --> 08:07.352
of your face on her
left butt cheek.

08:07.353 --> 08:09.621
Yeah, I kind of wish
she hadn't done that.

08:09.622 --> 08:11.156
After she takes a hot bath,

08:11.157 --> 08:13.292
I start looking like
Edward James Olmos.

08:13.293 --> 08:16.862
Just go over,
introduce yourself

08:16.863 --> 08:19.298
and welcome him to
the neighborhood.

08:19.299 --> 08:20.766
Yeah, I guess you're right.

08:20.767 --> 08:22.734
Bring over a bottle of wine,
little housewarming gift.

08:22.735 --> 08:24.703
Now you're talking.

08:24.704 --> 08:25.804
(clattering)

08:25.805 --> 08:27.105
JAKE and ELDRIDGE:
Geronimo!

08:27.106 --> 08:28.974
(both screaming)

08:28.975 --> 08:31.009
(crashing)

08:31.010 --> 08:33.045
Oh, God. Are you all right?

08:33.046 --> 08:34.479
JAKE:
Mostly.

08:34.480 --> 08:36.281
Did you remember
to get it on video?

08:36.282 --> 08:39.284
ELDRIDGE:
Aw, crap.

08:39.285 --> 08:42.354
♪ Men. ♪

08:44.591 --> 08:48.193
(doorbell rings)

08:48.194 --> 08:52.431
Charlie, what are
you doing here?

08:52.432 --> 08:53.465
I thought I'd stop by

08:53.466 --> 08:54.533
and welcome you guys
to the neighborhood.

08:54.534 --> 08:56.969
No, no. This is a
bad idea. Please go.

08:56.970 --> 08:58.136
But I thought we could
open a bottle of wine

08:58.137 --> 08:59.271
and all get
to know each other.

08:59.272 --> 09:00.672
Listen to me, Charlie.

09:00.673 --> 09:02.274
I love my husband.

09:02.275 --> 09:05.077
I'm building a new life with him
and I won't let you ruin it.

09:05.078 --> 09:06.478
How could I ruin it?

09:06.479 --> 09:08.013
Well, he doesn't
even know you exist,

09:08.014 --> 09:09.548
and I plan on
keeping it that way.

09:09.549 --> 09:11.583
How is that possible?
What about the tattoo?

09:11.584 --> 09:15.153
I added glasses to it and
told him it was Harry Potter.

09:17.490 --> 09:19.691
Now, please get out of here.

09:19.692 --> 09:22.127
Okay, fine.

09:22.128 --> 09:24.379
I'm sorry.

09:24.380 --> 09:28.033
Just so I'm clear,
you and I, we're...?

09:28.034 --> 09:30.302
Over, finished.

09:30.303 --> 09:32.704
Okay.

09:32.705 --> 09:34.573
I get it.

09:41.197 --> 09:43.365
Told you he'd stop by.

09:45.551 --> 09:47.369
♪ Men. ♪

09:47.370 --> 09:49.655
Do you realize how
lucky you are?

09:49.656 --> 09:50.989
You could have
broken your necks.

09:50.990 --> 09:53.358
We took precautions.

09:57.363 --> 09:59.831
You flew off the roof!

10:01.100 --> 10:03.702
In a shopping cart!

10:05.838 --> 10:07.139
What precautions?

10:07.140 --> 10:10.876
We were planning
to land in the ocean.

10:12.378 --> 10:16.281
You missed it by 100 yards.

10:16.282 --> 10:19.718
It's not an exact science, Dad.

10:19.719 --> 10:22.354
Okay, okay. Let's not
dicker over the details.

10:22.355 --> 10:23.438
(both laughing)

10:23.439 --> 10:25.257
He said, "dicker."

10:25.258 --> 10:26.792
I know.

10:26.793 --> 10:28.660
Okay, okay.
I am serious. Okay?

10:28.661 --> 10:30.829
This &lt;i>Dumbass&lt;/i> thing
stops right now.

10:30.830 --> 10:33.165
You're the one who told me
I should follow my dreams.

10:33.166 --> 10:36.168
I meant dreams
like "doctor" or "lawyer,"

10:36.169 --> 10:38.070
not "crash test dummy."

10:39.872 --> 10:43.308
"Dr. Jacob Harper."
I like the sound of that.

10:43.309 --> 10:46.578
Hey, doc, what's this on
my nutsack? Is it infected?

10:48.815 --> 10:52.517
Yes. It seems we'll have to
perform a nutsackectomy.

10:52.518 --> 10:53.719
(both chuckling)

10:53.720 --> 10:55.921
Will you two quit

10:55.922 --> 10:58.473
with the cockamamie babble

10:58.474 --> 11:01.159
and focus on what
I am trying to tell you?

11:01.160 --> 11:04.096
He said, "cockamamie."

11:04.097 --> 11:06.114
(both laughing)

11:06.115 --> 11:07.499
He said, "focus."

11:07.500 --> 11:08.934
(laughter)

11:12.205 --> 11:14.306
♪ Men. ♪

11:14.307 --> 11:16.508
(TV plays quietly)

11:17.844 --> 11:20.479
Oh, what's to become
of my son?

11:22.298 --> 11:24.483
Don't worry, Alan.

11:24.484 --> 11:26.651
There'll always be carnivals.

11:28.421 --> 11:30.088
I suppose.

11:30.089 --> 11:33.258
So, how'd it go
with Mr. and Mrs. Manfred Quinn?

11:33.259 --> 11:36.094
I never met him.
Rose told me to get lost.

11:36.095 --> 11:38.897
Wow. That's got to sting a bit.

11:38.898 --> 11:40.365
Yeah, but I understand.

11:40.366 --> 11:42.834
She's happy now, and doesn't
want me screwing it up.

11:42.835 --> 11:45.537
You still love her, don't you?

11:46.372 --> 11:48.740
I guess I do.

11:48.741 --> 11:51.810
Funny how these things turn out,
isn't it?

11:51.811 --> 11:54.146
I mean, eight, nine years ago,

11:54.147 --> 11:56.548
she was just a crazy
one-night stand

11:56.549 --> 11:58.750
who ended up stalking you.

12:00.253 --> 12:02.754
All you wanted
to do was get rid of her.

12:02.755 --> 12:04.189
But the years go by,

12:04.190 --> 12:07.793
and stalking turns
to friendship.

12:09.328 --> 12:11.763
Friendship turns to love.

12:12.999 --> 12:15.000
But it's too late.

12:15.001 --> 12:17.969
She marries another man,
and she's lost to you forever.

12:19.906 --> 12:22.607
Boy, that would make
a great movie, wouldn't it?

12:22.608 --> 12:24.910
Yeah, great.

12:24.911 --> 12:26.645
Want to write it with me?

12:26.646 --> 12:28.380
What?! No!

12:28.381 --> 12:31.516
Well, don't go stealing it.

12:32.652 --> 12:33.852
I mean, you know,

12:33.853 --> 12:35.420
it's your life,
but it's my idea.

12:35.421 --> 12:37.289
(sighs)

12:37.290 --> 12:39.224
Oh, how's this
for a title?

12:39.225 --> 12:41.760
&lt;i>Look Who's Stalking.&lt;/i>

12:42.962 --> 12:46.531
&lt;i>Meet the Stalkers.&lt;/i>

12:48.568 --> 12:50.802
&lt;i>Avatart.&lt;/i>

12:51.704 --> 12:53.205
Are you done?

12:53.206 --> 12:54.539
Yeah.

12:54.540 --> 12:57.576
Although I do think it has
real franchise opportunities.

12:57.577 --> 13:00.111
Could be a sitcom.

13:00.112 --> 13:04.649
Maybe not on a major network,
but, you know, TBS, TNT.

13:06.552 --> 13:09.554
&lt;i>I Love Looney.&lt;/i>

13:11.524 --> 13:13.391
Where you going?

13:13.392 --> 13:15.293
I was just spitballin' here.

13:18.731 --> 13:20.699
(quietly chuckling)

13:20.700 --> 13:22.667
I said, "spitballin'."

13:22.668 --> 13:24.870
(quietly chuckling)

13:25.705 --> 13:28.573
Oh, God, I want to die.

13:28.574 --> 13:31.409
♪ Men. ♪

13:31.410 --> 13:33.778
(slow, romantic
music plays on TV)

13:43.289 --> 13:46.224
♪ Men. ♪

13:48.261 --> 13:51.296
♪ Men. ♪

13:56.748 --> 13:58.876
That has got to be
the worst-looking toupee

13:58.976 --> 14:01.144
I've ever seen.

14:01.145 --> 14:03.079
What the hell
are you doing here?!

14:03.080 --> 14:05.682
You scared the
hell out of me.

14:05.683 --> 14:08.018
Are you crazy,
climbing up on my deck,

14:08.019 --> 14:09.853
snooping around like this?!

14:10.688 --> 14:12.756
I need to talk to you.

14:12.757 --> 14:14.557
Well, I can't
talk to you.

14:14.558 --> 14:15.825
Manny is right inside.

14:15.826 --> 14:17.861
I love you.
It's a little late for that.

14:17.862 --> 14:20.530
I'm sorry. I realize now, Rose,
I can't live without you.

14:20.531 --> 14:22.065
It doesn't matter
what you realize.

14:22.066 --> 14:23.166
I'm married now.

14:23.167 --> 14:24.367
Oh, please, Rose.

14:24.368 --> 14:25.602
Oh, God, Charlie,

14:25.603 --> 14:27.621
why are you doing this
to me? It's so unfair.

14:27.622 --> 14:29.706
I'm begging you.
Just talk to me.

14:29.707 --> 14:31.441
(sighs)

14:31.442 --> 14:33.143
All right.

14:33.144 --> 14:36.546
Manny has to go back into
the office to do some work.

14:36.547 --> 14:38.515
Come back in an hour.
Thank you.

14:38.516 --> 14:39.950
But just to talk.
Of course.

14:39.951 --> 14:43.486
- And can you bring me some
butter brickle ice cream?
- What?

14:43.487 --> 14:46.056
- And marshmallow fluff and sprinkles.
- Sure, whatever you need.

14:46.057 --> 14:48.058
Chocolate sprinkles, not
the multicolored kind.

14:48.059 --> 14:50.360
- Fine. 
- I don't know why they even make those.

14:50.361 --> 14:51.895
Okay.
Okay.

14:51.896 --> 14:53.463
I'll see you later.

14:53.464 --> 14:55.598
(thudding)
Ow!

14:55.599 --> 14:57.567
Son of a bitch!
How do you do that?

14:57.568 --> 15:00.337
Don't lock your knees.

15:03.541 --> 15:05.875
(romantic music plays on TV)

15:06.911 --> 15:08.811
Good news, Manny.

15:08.812 --> 15:10.813
We're getting ice cream.

15:14.535 --> 15:16.819
♪ Men. ♪

15:16.820 --> 15:18.955
You ready
for some more beans?

15:18.956 --> 15:21.124
Bring it on.

15:21.125 --> 15:22.625
(clears throat)

15:22.626 --> 15:26.363
So, I'm thinking we call
this stunt "Fart Rocket."

15:26.364 --> 15:30.233
Nah, I think we need to go with
something more intellectual.

15:30.234 --> 15:33.770
How about
"The Dumbass Assblaster?"

15:33.771 --> 15:36.606
No, you can't use
two "asses" in a row.

15:36.607 --> 15:39.693
It's... redumbnant.

15:39.694 --> 15:42.412
Hey.

15:42.413 --> 15:43.947
What's going on?

15:43.948 --> 15:45.815
I'm just making Eldridge
something to eat.

15:45.816 --> 15:48.151
Really?

15:48.152 --> 15:51.254
Yes, I was peckerish.

15:53.324 --> 15:55.759
You mean peckish.

15:55.760 --> 15:58.361
Fine. If you
want to dicker.

15:58.362 --> 15:59.695
(both laughing)

15:59.696 --> 16:02.432
Good one, dude.

16:05.836 --> 16:07.587
Hey.

16:07.588 --> 16:09.472
What's in the bag?

16:09.473 --> 16:11.057
Butter brickle ice cream

16:11.058 --> 16:13.910
with marshmallow fluff
and chocolate sprinkles.

16:13.911 --> 16:15.278
Oh, Charlie, no.

16:15.279 --> 16:17.247
What?!

16:17.248 --> 16:19.115
"What?!"

16:19.116 --> 16:21.518
Only one person on earth
puts chocolate sprinkles

16:21.519 --> 16:23.853
and marshmallow fluff on
butter brickle ice cream.

16:23.854 --> 16:25.188
Congratulations, Sherlock.

16:25.189 --> 16:26.889
You cracked the case.

16:26.890 --> 16:28.608
She is a married woman, Charlie.

16:28.609 --> 16:30.527
I can't help it. I love her.

16:30.528 --> 16:32.162
Oh, please.
You didn't start loving her

16:32.163 --> 16:33.963
until you found out
you couldn't have her.

16:33.964 --> 16:37.500
So? That doesn't
make it... &lt;i>not&lt;/i> love.

16:37.501 --> 16:39.502
But what if her husband
catches you?

16:39.503 --> 16:41.204
Then he shoots me, and you can
have my house and my car.

16:41.205 --> 16:44.641
Go to her, Charlie.
She's waiting.

16:48.112 --> 16:50.213
(sighs)

16:50.214 --> 16:51.614
(thudding)
Ow!

16:51.615 --> 16:53.650
Son of a bitch!

16:53.651 --> 16:56.319
(breaking wind)

16:56.320 --> 16:58.354
JAKE:
Dude, don't waste it.

16:58.355 --> 17:00.557
Squeeze it in!

17:03.027 --> 17:05.195
♪ Men. ♪

17:05.196 --> 17:07.597
(panting)

17:11.202 --> 17:13.236
(grunting)

17:13.237 --> 17:16.272
Not as easy
as it looks, is it?

17:16.273 --> 17:17.824
No.

17:17.825 --> 17:19.609
Is your husband gone?

17:19.610 --> 17:20.943
He just left.
We're alone.

17:20.944 --> 17:23.046
Oh, great.
Wait.

17:23.047 --> 17:24.547
We agreed, just talking.

17:24.548 --> 17:26.850
Right, right, right.
Just talking. Let's talk.

17:26.851 --> 17:29.252
Do you know what Manny said
to me right before he left?

17:29.253 --> 17:30.920
Um... "I love you,

17:30.921 --> 17:33.456
"but it's okay to have
an affair with Charlie,

17:33.457 --> 17:35.925
'cause he's a swell guy
and I'm secretly gay"?

17:35.926 --> 17:37.527
No.

17:37.528 --> 17:39.129
He said, in the whole world,

17:39.130 --> 17:42.098
I'm the only one
who can move him.

17:42.933 --> 17:44.934
Like I said, gay.

17:44.935 --> 17:48.304
How can I betray
a man like that?

17:48.305 --> 17:50.006
I can think of
several ways.

17:50.007 --> 17:52.909
You on top, you on bottom,
everybody facing the TV.

17:52.910 --> 17:54.344
Charlie.

17:54.345 --> 17:57.347
Who moves you,
Rose? Him or me?

17:57.348 --> 17:59.149
I don't know. I'm confused.

17:59.150 --> 18:00.416
I love Manny.

18:00.417 --> 18:03.052
But you and I are soul mates,
like Romeo and Juliet.

18:03.053 --> 18:05.522
Really? Did Romeo ever
chew through the ropes

18:05.523 --> 18:08.391
holding him to a radiator in
a motel outside of Bakersfield

18:08.392 --> 18:11.427
when Juliet was just trying
to give him a birthday surprise?

18:11.428 --> 18:13.997
Birthday surprise? You
were going to brand me.

18:13.998 --> 18:16.533
Branding is the new
piercing, Charlie.

18:16.534 --> 18:20.403
Fine. Pierce me, brand me,
do anything you want.

18:20.404 --> 18:22.555
Anything?
It's just an expression.

18:24.441 --> 18:26.075
Give me another chance, Rose.

18:26.076 --> 18:28.611
No. It's wrong.

18:28.612 --> 18:31.748
Fine. You just say the
word, and I'll go.

18:33.984 --> 18:35.018
Time's up.

18:35.019 --> 18:37.570
(sighing)

18:37.571 --> 18:38.688
I love you.

18:38.689 --> 18:40.790
I love you, too.

18:40.791 --> 18:42.992
You know what this means,
don't you?

18:42.993 --> 18:45.027
I think so.

18:45.028 --> 18:46.796
You're going to have
to kill Manny.

18:46.797 --> 18:49.232
What?!

18:49.233 --> 18:50.667
Kidding.

18:50.668 --> 18:53.002
Just wanted to see
how far you'd go.

18:54.672 --> 18:57.039
♪ Men. ♪

18:57.040 --> 18:59.042
Can I tell you
something, Rose?

18:59.043 --> 19:00.643
Anything.

19:00.644 --> 19:03.179
I've never felt happier
and more at peace

19:03.180 --> 19:04.981
than I do
at this very moment.

19:04.982 --> 19:08.217
Who's being a
little gay now?

19:16.193 --> 19:18.394
(phone chimes)

19:21.365 --> 19:22.966
Oh. It's a text from Manny.

19:22.967 --> 19:25.618
He's on his way home.
You have to go.

19:26.870 --> 19:28.421
When can I see you again?

19:28.422 --> 19:30.239
You can't.
This was a mistake.

19:30.240 --> 19:31.541
How can you say that?

19:31.542 --> 19:33.743
Charlie, I love my husband.

19:33.744 --> 19:35.428
Forget Manny.
Run away with me.

19:35.429 --> 19:36.679
You don't mean that.

19:36.680 --> 19:37.547
I do.

19:37.548 --> 19:38.715
Come on, Charlie.

19:38.716 --> 19:39.882
If you had me to yourself,

19:39.883 --> 19:41.484
you'd be tired of me
within a year.

19:41.485 --> 19:43.486
Then you can go back to Manny.
Everybody wins.

19:46.256 --> 19:47.757
Go.

19:48.959 --> 19:51.144
I love you.

19:57.835 --> 20:01.237
Oh, aren't you the naughty boy
who likes to watch?

20:01.238 --> 20:03.606
♪ Men. ♪

20:05.354 --> 20:06.487
♪ Men. ♪

20:06.488 --> 20:07.722
ELDRIDGE:
Hurry up, dude.

20:07.723 --> 20:09.623
I'm about to blow.
Hang on.

20:11.226 --> 20:13.427
Hi. I'm Jake Harper,

20:13.428 --> 20:14.628
and you're about to witness

20:14.629 --> 20:17.198
a little something
we like to call...

20:17.199 --> 20:20.368
"Fumes of Fury."

20:20.369 --> 20:23.444
- Let's do this thing.
- All right.

20:23.869 --> 20:25.169
Remember, if
for some reason

20:25.170 --> 20:27.254
you don't reach the
ocean, just tuck and roll.

20:27.255 --> 20:28.539
Okay, just hurry up.

20:28.540 --> 20:31.175
All right.
Let 'er rip.

20:31.176 --> 20:33.632
(breaking wind,
flame roaring)

20:38.712 --> 20:39.912
Dumbasses.

20:42.859 --> 20:44.236
I can't believe nothing happened.

20:44.436 --> 20:45.636
I wouldn't say that.

20:45.836 --> 20:47.176
I think I cracked my pants.

20:49.251 --> 20:51.712
♪ Men. ♪

20:51.812 --> 20:54.812
 == Sync, corrected by &lt;font color="#00ff00">elderman&lt;/font> ==
